# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/upload-1 window (docs/tp4-upload1.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-1-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed head of tp4/upload-1 (the ship-5 stack plus the host tier's upload levers, qwen_tier_upload;
# substitute it in every template with one command: sed -i 's/tp4-upload-1-1/<tag>/' *.env). THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that exists. The levers live in files the image carries
# (qwen_tier_upload.py, qwen_prefix_registry.py, qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py): an image built before them ignores the three names and the arm reads NOT_EXERCISED (no "host tier upload on" line).
# The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent (production is down by the owner's choice while it runs).
# F1 (MEASURE, soft): the four-card host-to-device re-measure that locates the 23.9 GB/s cap (tp4_h2d_probe.py, docs/tp4-fabric-upload.md 6.5; the arms are on this branch since the merge of
# tp4/fabric-upload). Alone and together as in run 38036227448, plus the arms that were added for the cap: chunked/together (the same bytes per card in calls under the 32 MiB pinned threshold: 8 MiB a card,
# 32 MiB in all), chunked/alone (each card in 16 MiB calls), threads (one Python thread per card writing its own card with the one-coordinate write) and threads_busy (per-thread host CPU).
# READ: 'H2D_PROBE verdict=MEASURED' (INEXACT = a shard holds bytes nobody wrote: stop; PARTIAL = read the problems lines). THE QUESTIONS, answered by the verdict line and the arms, never by this header:
# (1) does chunked/together beat together (23.9 GB/s) - then the cap is the pinned zero-copy path above 32 MiB and the call size is the lever (U7 and U8 then sweep it on the real restore: the registry knob
# QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_CHUNK_BLOCKS); (2) do the four threads beat one - the dispatch already runs one thread per card (mesh_command_queue_base.cpp:261-266), so a gain here means the Python call
# serialised them; (3) threads_busy: is one host thread saturated during the together arm. Measurement only: no model is loaded and nothing is served; a failed run needs a reset first.
# Estimate: 30 minutes (reset 3-12 plus the probe 8-20).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=h2d
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-1-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=45
